e image area once there is an image\n\nThe preview claimed every touch over itself for as long as a finger was down,\nso that a pan or a pinch could not be stolen by the ScrollView it sits in.\nWith no image picked that left 260dp of the page that could not be scrolled\npast - the area shows \"No image\" and there is nothing in it to place, so the\ndrag belongs to the page. It now hands those touches straight on, by the same\ntest onDraw uses to decide it has nothing to show, and takes the gesture back\nthe moment an image is in. An image that disappears mid-gesture releases the\nScrollView right away, because the ACTION_UP that normally does it only\nreaches a view that still claims the touch.\n\nThe gesture tests check both directions now. For the ones that need a picture,\na debuggable build takes a generated one from the launch intent\n(--ez oepl_test_image true); the only other way in is the system photo picker,\nwhich is another app's UI and different on every phone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MjB1jUoctE9vxpyRA7nhQt\n"}